  "notes": "TRUE PROGRAM NAME: Bristol Community College offers this as 'Computer Science Transfer' (program code CI_CIX), a concentration of the Computer Information Systems major, Academic Area: Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics, Type: Associate in Science (CIP 11.0701). There is no plainly-named 'Computer Science' degree; this is the college's true CS degree (prepares for transfer into a 4-year Computer Science program; seamless transfer path to UMass Dartmouth Computer Science). Source: Bristol Community College Academic Catalog 2026-2027, 'Computer Science Transfer' program page, 'Recommended Course Sequence' (Semester 1-4). Transcribed manually from the college's own catalog PDF (labeled '2026-27 Catalog' on every page): the live catalog.bristolcc.edu homepage confirms the current Academic Catalog is 2026-2027, but the per-program 2026-27 PDF had not yet been published at the live path at transcription time (2026-09-30), so the identical content was taken from the college's own catalog staging host (test-bristol-catalog.pantheonsite.io), same Coursedog/Pantheon catalog CMS as catalog.bristolcc.edu. Program details cross-checked against the college's official Registrar program list (bristolcc.edu/learnatbristol/academicresources/registrarrecords/). CREDIT TOTAL: the catalog prints 'Total credits: 70-71'. The range comes from the Semester 4 choice 'MTH 244 or CIS 266' (3-4 cr): MTH 244 Discrete Structures II is 3 cr, CIS 266 Data Structures is 4 cr. This plan uses the 3-credit base path (MTH 244); the sequence sums to exactly 70 = 17+17+18+18. Choosing CIS 266 instead brings the plan to 71. PREREQS: the official Recommended Course Sequence does not print prerequisites term-by-term, so all prereq lists are empty rather than invented. CAVEAT: the 2025-26 version of this program differed (two-course history sequence, Human Expression elective, no COM 104, no CIS 266 option); this file is the 2026-27 revision.",
